    "result_text": "I agreed with the finding and applied it. Tests are green.\n\n## Changes\n\nI extracted the inlined `else if` into a dedicated `assertRegistrationDateNotInFuture(owner)` helper that mirrors the three existing sibling guards (`assertIdentityIsUnique`, `assertCityHasCapacity`, `assertDailyRegistrationLimit`) \u2014 same shape, same domain-exception throw, placed right next to them. `saveOwner` now reads as a flat sequence of asserts, with validation cleanly separated from the null-defaulting block:\n\n```java\nif (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {\n    owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());\n}\nassertRegistrationDateNotInFuture(owner);\nowner.setRegistrationDate(rollToBusinessDay(owner.getRegistrationDate()));\n```\n\nAs the review noted, calling the check after defaulting is safe: a defaulted `LocalDate.now()` is never `isAfter(now())`, so the null case stays a no-op. The exception class and handler were untouched (the review had no concerns there). Full `./mvnw test` build passes.",
